{"sha":"497c81c1f5016dc6ef5b3219ece2f3c261d4d8f1","node_id":"C_kwDOAaBqHNoAKDQ5N2M4MWMxZjUwMTZkYzZlZjViMzIxOWVjZTJmM2MyNjFkNGQ4ZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Andrew Waterman","email":"aswaterman@gmail.com","date":"2026-10-23T23:48:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-23T23:48:46Z"},"message":"Fix build on Apple Clang 21 with -Wuninitialized-const-pointer (#48)\n\nThe RISC-V port neither initializes nor consumes the commonNaN\nstruct, but this raises Clang's hackles when const pointers to\nthese uninitialized structs are passed.\n\nFix by initializing the struct.  This has no performance impact\nsince the callees are always inlined.\n\nSee #46\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrew Waterman <andrew@sifive.com>","tree":{"sha":"58c5bcd148e5879f83aea1544df48ab90aad5fcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ucb-bar/berkeley-softfloat-3/git/trees/58c5bcd148e5879f83aea1544df48ab90aad5fcb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ucb-bar/berkeley-softfloat-3/git/commits/497c81c1f5016dc6ef5b3219ece2f3c261d4d8f1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq2/JeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPiEQAGwN7bvYbfcfKjFQfj6789bW\nyYr4HPbpjF1h26Q/WVjImeCXIMvPDwwzTueQrhd0B/9rccnYW2gteaK30vSMSv/k\nZwq0TtPgMLnyuax7Ve/WOY59hUH+gVmtwDl3GZWDwGBF8nDSEaq9Scga9mscUrWK\nXFv4/TX3p4SVK+s/ZmXYuffvzYhaRa5zHqEQauR7nekKALbBcTGBwW83skOwHLj2\nrBed6Pf9gsSXbnCpCeObYayrfjHQZQayzIAuZjrYPPjEd7PKPhx1FtehY6Y+AbhO\njjTf9xyVS+t/eyvdk1R2LiKnXZDp7D82YMRR/2f7SvNHyTOtv2cshtIBgN/EbtPN\nHUIM6ou+d3ESACr53pgVLtK7qAmEQNjrLEbCLVKM982IvwXkbrrhAu6OrXQltokS\nTn3aTTsbwOV6oS/eIXy99TJsQh0pDr5qgjeGPVEHYC0zdRB6ZFH15W/YFgBp4GdJ\nmeHzOWgkk8iRL6pXOhDmw0fsZmNVsEsUkNEZUwnlBSYELh1TSzorsFXCa2GCwT8C\nQjqHUCGl6XRKRVfxq2+xaEBjQhJhqLC4RhWTJ2L1+EUoM2WJ2HYpfKeI6koXcowm\n2ueA8Fv9AG9NaMNWfNDXLjsYR7cF1w0JOGDjxXG0LLY18mDwiW1e9yekxZJS9HhO\n+09RYAlDfBzjADMhLjJP\n=nczK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 58c5bcd148e5879f83aea1544df48ab90aad5fcb\nparent 5d28716af040943b2a8852a0c1089562d8f22d78\nauthor Andrew Waterman <aswaterman@gmail.com> 1792799326 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792799326 -0700\n\nFix build on Apple Clang 21 with -Wuninitialized-const-pointer (#48)\n\nThe RISC-V port neither initializes nor consumes the commonNaN\nstruct, but this raises Clang's hackles when const pointers to\nthese uninitialized structs are passed.\n\nFix by initializing the struct.  This has no performance impact\nsince the callees are always inlined.\n\nSee #46\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrew Waterman <andrew@sifive.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-23T23:48:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ucb-bar/berkeley-softfloat-3/commits/497c81c1f5016dc6ef5b3219ece2f3c261d4d8f1","html_url":"https://github.com/ucb-bar/berkeley-softfloat-3/commit/497c81c1f5016dc6ef5b3219ece2f3c261d4d8f1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ucb-bar/berkeley-softfloat-3/commits/497c81c1f5016dc6ef5b3219ece2f3c261d4d8f1/comments","author":{"login":"aswaterman","id":1031106,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzExMDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1031106?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aswaterman","html_url":"https://github.com/aswaterman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aswaterman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aswaterman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aswaterman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aswaterman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aswaterman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aswaterman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aswaterman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aswaterman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aswaterman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5d28716af040943b2a8852a0c1089562d8f22d78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ucb-bar/berkeley-softfloat-3/commits/5d28716af040943b2a8852a0c1089562d8f22d78","html_url":"https://github.com/ucb-bar/berkeley-softfloat-3/commit/5d28716af040943b2a8852a0c1089562d8f22d78"}],"stats":{"total":16,"additions":8,"deletions":8},"files":[{"sha":"931d796e28fc220ee7adaed938c7a25859407668","filename":"source/RISCV/specialize.h","status":"modified","additions":8,"deletions":8,"changes":16,"blob_url":"https://github.com/ucb-bar/berkeley-softfloat-3/blob/497c81c1f5016dc6ef5b3219ece2f3c261d4d8f1/source%2FRISCV%2Fspecialize.h","raw_url":"https://github.com/ucb-bar/berkeley-softfloat-3/raw/497c81c1f5016dc6ef5b3219ece2f3c261d4d8f1/source%2FRISCV%2Fspecialize.h","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ucb-bar/berkeley-softfloat-3/contents/source%2FRISCV%2Fspecialize.h?ref=497c81c1f5016dc6ef5b3219ece2f3c261d4d8f1","patch":"@@ -100,15 +100,15 @@ struct commonNaN { char _unused; };\n | location pointed to by 'zPtr'.  If the NaN is a signaling NaN, the invalid\n | exception is raised.\n *----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n-#define softfloat_f16UIToCommonNaN( uiA, zPtr ) if ( ! ((uiA) & 0x0200) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid )\n+#define softfloat_f16UIToCommonNaN( uiA, zPtr ) do { (zPtr)->_unused = 0; if ( ! ((uiA) & 0x0200) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid ); } while (0)\n \n /*----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n | Assuming 'uiA' has the bit pattern of a 16-bit BF16 floating-point NaN, converts\n | this NaN to the common NaN form, and stores the resulting common NaN at the\n | location pointed to by 'zPtr'.  If the NaN is a signaling NaN, the invalid\n | exception is raised.\n *----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n-#define softfloat_bf16UIToCommonNaN( uiA, zPtr ) if ( ! ((uiA) & 0x0040) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid )\n+#define softfloat_bf16UIToCommonNaN( uiA, zPtr ) do { (zPtr)->_unused = 0; if ( ! ((uiA) & 0x0040) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid ); } while (0)\n \n /*----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n | Converts the common NaN pointed to by 'aPtr' into a 16-bit floating-point\n@@ -154,7 +154,7 @@ uint_fast16_t\n | location pointed to by 'zPtr'.  If the NaN is a signaling NaN, the invalid\n | exception is raised.\n *----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n-#define softfloat_f32UIToCommonNaN( uiA, zPtr ) if ( ! ((uiA) & 0x00400000) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid )\n+#define softfloat_f32UIToCommonNaN( uiA, zPtr ) do { (zPtr)->_unused = 0; if ( ! ((uiA) & 0x00400000) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid ); } while (0)\n \n /*----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n | Converts the common NaN pointed to by 'aPtr' into a 32-bit floating-point\n@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@ uint_fast32_t\n | location pointed to by 'zPtr'.  If the NaN is a signaling NaN, the invalid\n | exception is raised.\n *----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n-#define softfloat_f64UIToCommonNaN( uiA, zPtr ) if ( ! ((uiA) & UINT64_C( 0x0008000000000000 )) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid )\n+#define softfloat_f64UIToCommonNaN( uiA, zPtr ) do { (zPtr)->_unused = 0; if ( ! ((uiA) & UINT64_C( 0x0008000000000000 )) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid ); } while (0)\n \n /*----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n | Converts the common NaN pointed to by 'aPtr' into a 64-bit floating-point\n@@ -234,7 +234,7 @@ uint_fast64_t\n | location pointed to by 'zPtr'.  If the NaN is a signaling NaN, the invalid\n | exception is raised.\n *----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n-#define softfloat_extF80UIToCommonNaN( uiA64, uiA0, zPtr ) if ( ! ((uiA0) & UINT64_C( 0x4000000000000000 )) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid )\n+#define softfloat_extF80UIToCommonNaN( uiA64, uiA0, zPtr ) do { (zPtr)->_unused = 0; if ( ! ((uiA0) & UINT64_C( 0x4000000000000000 )) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid ); } while (0)\n \n /*----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n | Converts the common NaN pointed to by 'aPtr' into an 80-bit extended\n@@ -292,7 +292,7 @@ struct uint128\n | pointed to by 'zPtr'.  If the NaN is a signaling NaN, the invalid exception\n | is raised.\n *----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n-#define softfloat_f128UIToCommonNaN( uiA64, uiA0, zPtr ) if ( ! ((uiA64) & UINT64_C( 0x0000800000000000 )) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid )\n+#define softfloat_f128UIToCommonNaN( uiA64, uiA0, zPtr ) do { (zPtr)->_unused = 0; if ( ! ((uiA64) & UINT64_C( 0x0000800000000000 )) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid ); } while (0)\n \n /*----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n | Converts the common NaN pointed to by 'aPtr' into a 128-bit floating-point\n@@ -341,7 +341,7 @@ struct uint128\n | common NaN at the location pointed to by 'zPtr'.  If the NaN is a signaling\n | NaN, the invalid exception is raised.\n *----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n-#define softfloat_extF80MToCommonNaN( aSPtr, zPtr ) if ( ! ((aSPtr)->signif & UINT64_C( 0x4000000000000000 )) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid )\n+#define softfloat_extF80MToCommonNaN( aSPtr, zPtr ) do { (zPtr)->_unused = 0; if ( ! ((aSPtr)->signif & UINT64_C( 0x4000000000000000 )) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid ); } while (0)\n \n /*----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n | Converts the common NaN pointed to by 'aPtr' into an 80-bit extended\n@@ -392,7 +392,7 @@ void\n | four 32-bit elements that concatenate in the platform's normal endian order\n | to form a 128-bit floating-point value.\n *----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n-#define softfloat_f128MToCommonNaN( aWPtr, zPtr ) if ( ! ((aWPtr)[indexWordHi( 4 )] & UINT64_C( 0x0000800000000000 )) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid )\n+#define softfloat_f128MToCommonNaN( aWPtr, zPtr ) do { (zPtr)->_unused = 0; if ( ! ((aWPtr)[indexWordHi( 4 )] & UINT64_C( 0x0000800000000000 )) ) softfloat_raiseFlags( softfloat_flag_invalid ); } while (0)\n \n /*----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n | Converts the common NaN pointed to by 'aPtr' into a 128-bit floating-point"}]}